SCALE-THREE HAMMING-SIX DEPTH-THREE GEOMETRY-BATCH PROTOTYPE
Date: 2026-07-15
Status: exact bounded implementation/benchmark; not a full census and not an
emptiness claim.

SOURCE
04-computation/lrc13_scale_three_hamming_six_depth_three_geometry_batch_codex_S16.cpp
SHA-256 5b53b1cad43ac30a7c2b12c7a5fdb97513c449c10f832f7d38a190118823bc4f

DESIGN
The imported S16 depth-two engine reconstructs the 1,504 CRT contexts and
supplies the exact rational predicates.  Contexts are processed one root mask
at a time.  Logical depth-two lanes are transposed first by (R,x1,x2), then by
proposed x3.  The literal parent/child component geometry is evaluated once
per metric key and discarded immediately after all attached lanes consume it.

Every attached lane still carries context index, used-label mask, labelled x1,
labelled x2, proposed labelled x3, least later ray, and shortcut verdict.  Thus
the cache is not a proof-state quotient.  The complete-tooth predicate is
metric; the streaming-cap predicate is re-evaluated with the lane-specific
least future ray.

The speed-s comb intersection is streamed through only the teeth overlapping
each current component.  It never retains all s safe bands.  With
--literal-crosscheck, every streamed intersection is compared endpoint by
endpoint with the original materialized-safe-band routine.

REPRESENTATIVE SAME-ROOT BENCHMARK
Command:
  /usr/bin/time -l /tmp/c3-d3-batch \
    --context-start 20 --context-limit 8 --mode compare --gate-audit

The eight contexts are indices 20,...,27 inside the 36-context root-mask 2199
block (stratum 2,4).  Both engines returned:
  logical depth1 = 568
  logical depth2 = 40,680
  logical depth3 = 1,685,358
  full-tooth depth3 = 1,542,729
  streaming-dead depth3 = 138,945
  materialized/live depth3 = 3,684
  covering depth3 = 0
  lane fingerprint xor = 92e6871df66247b0
  lane fingerprint sum = 159352585f8e7074
  per-context rows equal = yes

Literal/raw metric calls versus batch metric calls:
  depth1: 568 -> 143
  depth2: 40,680 -> 17,447
  depth3 (after tooth gate): 142,629 -> 86,316
  unique (R,x1,x2,x3) keys, including teeth: 1,039,782

Measured in the same process under concurrent repository load:
  raw wall / CPU = 22.0156 / 11.8168 seconds
  batch wall / CPU = 13.1800 / 7.38807 seconds
  wall speedup = 1.67038
  CPU speedup = 1.59944
  maximum resident set size for the combined raw+batch process = 6,995,968 B
  peak memory footprint = 7,374,080 B

The timings are a benchmark, not a bound.  The exact call counts and logical
fingerprints are the reproducible content.

LITERAL-ARITHMETIC AND BUILD CHECKS
Context 103 (the light 2,4 pilot) was run in compare mode with both
--gate-audit and --literal-crosscheck.  All streamed comb intersections matched
the original materialized-band routine.  Raw and batch both returned:
  depth1,depth2,depth3 = 53,3,011,97,386
  tooth,stream,materialized,cover = 87,184,9,629,573,0
  fingerprint xor = 8eac81632173e3a4
  fingerprint sum = 1e20bb79dde005cc

Warning-clean -O0 and -O3 builds gave byte-identical output after removing the
four timing fields.  An AddressSanitizer+UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer build ran
the batch/literal-crosscheck pilot cleanly (leak detection disabled because it
is unsupported by the platform ASan runtime).

TOURNAMENT AUDIT
Vertices are the remaining labelled rays, not metric geometries.  The pair
observable is the difference of least legal step-39 speeds after the prefix;
the numerical-order switch orients the edge, with increasing label as the
unused tie realizer.  Every conditioned four-ray tournament is transitive:
score multiset 0,1,2,3; directed triangles 0; SCC profile 1,1,1,1; one
Hamiltonian path.  The eight-context depth-two flip histogram against raw CRT
ray order is
  0:10,302  1:1,009  2:5,990  3:16,233  4:6,152  5:994  6:0
with 91,266 flips in total.  Geometry batching leaves this lane fingerprint
unchanged.

ALTERNATE-VERTEX ASSUMPTION AUDIT
Metric-prefix geometries are useful cache vertices, but not faithful proof
vertices.  They preserve exact residual circle components.  They destroy
label availability, the least future speed, the conditioned ray tournament,
and shortcut ancestry.  The faithful vertices remain labelled future-ray
obligations decorated by metric geometry and chronology.

RECOMMENDATION
Use complete root-mask blocks as independent shards.  Within each block retain
only the depth-one geometries and the depth-two lane ledger; reconstruct one
depth-two parent, transpose its proposed x3 values, consume its children, and
discard them.  This is the concrete bounded-memory route to the full gated
depth-three/full-depth census.  Do not merge lane states merely because their
metric prefix agrees.
